# asd

> A skill that circulates search results instead of leaving them in one chat.

## Purpose
Explain asd as a passer of search hits so they can move to the next reader or tool. Source: fitzyracing1/asd.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Take a search result.
2. Circulate it.
3. Do not bury it in one thread.

## Key ideas
- Search-result circulation (move hits onward)
- Skill (a small named behavior)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/asd
result = take_search_hit()
circulate(result)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. take_search_hit() → “accept one result”
2. circulate(result) → “pass it on”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a hit arrives → circulate it
- If nothing arrives → wait

## What a person would notice
Search hits leave the chat instead of sitting still.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open fitzyracing1/asd and pass one result through it.
